KG42.register("rules-ec063e88ece8a9cdb0e9c008",{"id":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R006","paper":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R006","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local clearing price","process_stage":"pricing","market_meaning":"Iterative price-signal coordination produces mutually agreed prices for local flexibility contracts. Scope: Bilateral flexibility contracts within the distribution-network market. Condition: At negotiation completion, when no price changes occur during an iteration. Each discrete unit of flexibility may be individually priced. Scope: Distribution-network flexibility contracts specifying equal energy quantities of demand reduction and discretizing flexibility in energy and time. Each trade is associated with at most one contract and therefore has a unique price. Scope: Individual flexibility trades in the distribution-network market. Condition: The selected contract set is a feasible market outcome.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function pricing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e24"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Bilateral flexibility contracts within the distribution-network market. | Distribution-network flexibility contracts specifying equal energy quantities of demand reduction and discretizing flexibility in energy and time. | Individual flexibility trades in the distribution-network market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e24"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-x001","symbol":"p^{b}_{\\omega}","meaning":"Buyer-side price of a flexibility trade ω during iterative price negotiation.","kind":"operational","domain":"price values assigned to each trade ω ∈ Ω; initialized to zero before negotiation and compared with the seller price during iterations","unit":null,"indices":["ω","iteration"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-x002","symbol":"p^{s}_{\\omega}","meaning":"Seller-side price of a flexibility trade ω during iterative price negotiation.","kind":"operational","domain":"price values assigned to each trade ω ∈ Ω; initialized to zero before negotiation and compared with the buyer price during iterations","unit":null,"indices":["ω","iteration"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-x003","symbol":"X'","meaning":"Selected feasible outcome set of contracts whose trades determine local contract prices.","kind":"operational","domain":"feasible sets of contracts X′ ⊆ X satisfying the source feasible-outcome condition","unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"]}],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Iterative price-signal coordination produces mutually agreed prices for local flexibility contracts. Scope: Bilateral flexibility contracts within the distribution-network market. Condition: At negotiation completion, when no price changes occur during an iteration.","expression":"\\forall \\omega \\in \\Omega:\\; p^{b,(k+1)}_{\\omega}=p^{b,(k)}_{\\omega}\\;\\land\\; p^{s,(k+1)}_{\\omega}=p^{s,(k)}_{\\omega}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-x001","v141-c-R006-x002"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e24","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each discrete unit of flexibility may be individually priced. Scope: Distribution-network flexibility contracts specifying equal energy quantities of demand reduction and discretizing flexibility in energy and time.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each trade is associated with at most one contract and therefore has a unique price. Scope: Individual flexibility trades in the distribution-network market. Condition: The selected contract set is a feasible market outcome.","expression":"\\forall \\omega \\in \\tau(X'):\\; |\\{(\\omega,t_{\\omega},p_{\\omega})\\in X'\\}| \\le 1","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-x003"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-12c011a9b5-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. Decentralized Flexibility Market Design","anchor_text":"eir their willingness to accept a contract specifying a price for a unit of of demand reduction duri","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Each contract specifies the same energy quantity of demand reduction, but an agent may accept multiple contracts for each time interval. The contracts discretize the prosumers’ energy flexibility (in terms of energy and time), and allow each discrete unit to be individually priced. Multi-interval trading is important, since prosumers may have storage systems with finite energy capacity. In this case, their willingness to accept a contract specifying a price for a unit of demand reduction during a particular interval will depend on the price and availability of contracts at other time intervals."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-12c011a9b5-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. Decentralized Flexibility Market Design","anchor_text":"eir their willingness to accept a contract specifying a price for a unit of of demand reduction duri","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The agents reach mutual agreement on a set of agreed contracts and contract prices through an iterative price-negotiation mechanism. At each step of the market, agents select their favorite bundle of available upstream and downstream contracts, and over-demanded contracts have their prices increased. The process continues until no price changes occur during an iteration."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-12c011a9b5-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Market Stability and Efficiency","anchor_text":"Uj(Yj ∪Zj) = −∞, otherwise (6) The aggregator preferences can be extended to handle sit- uations whe","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"For a trading network with contracts X, an outcome is a feasible set of contracts X' \\subseteq X, where X' is feasible if each trade \\omega \\in \\tau(X') is associated with at most one contract, and therefore has a unique price."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e24","location":{"location_id":"src-12c011a9b5-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.A Price-Negotiation Mechanism","anchor_text":"ON SYSTEM FLEXIBILITY 2133 The negotiation is complete when no price changes occur during an iterati","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The negotiation is complete when no price changes occur during an iteration. \\cup_{i\\in A} Y^{*}_i is a stable outcome for the trading network."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e21","location":{"location_id":"src-12c011a9b5-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.A Price-Negotiation Mechanism","anchor_text":"ω ∈Ω. The agents then engage in iterative negotiation with dow their neighbors. Each iteration: no r","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"A flow chart of the price-negotiation process is shown in Fig. 2. Each agent i \\in A starts by specifying the flexibility trades they may be willing to make. Let \\Omega be the full set of trades in the market. Each trade \\omega \\in \\Omega is assigned a buyer price p^{b}_{\\omega} and a seller price p^{s}_{\\omega}. Initially, p^{b}_{\\omega} = 0 and p^{s}_{\\omega} = 0 for all \\omega \\in \\Omega. The agents then engage in iterative negotiation with their neighbors. Each iteration: Each agent i \\in A constructs a set of upstream contracts to choose from, Y_i = \\{(\\omega, t_{\\omega}, p^{b}_{\\omega}) \\mid \\omega \\in \\Omega, b(\\omega) = i\\} and a set of downstream contracts to choose from, Z_i = \\{(\\omega, t_{\\omega}, p^{s}_{\\omega}) \\mid \\omega \\in \\Omega, s(\\omega) = i\\}."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-12c011a9b5-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.A Price-Negotiation Mechanism","anchor_text":"ω ∈Ω. The agents then engage in iterative negotiation with dow their neighbors. Each iteration: no r","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The prices of over-demanded trades are increased. The set of over-demanded trades is given by \\Phi = \\{\\omega \\in \\Omega \\mid (\\omega, t_{\\omega}, p_{\\omega}) \\in Y^{*}_{b(\\omega)}, \\omega \\notin Z^{*}_{s(\\omega)}\\}. For each \\omega \\in \\Phi, if p^{b}_{\\omega} > p^{s}_{\\omega}, then p^{s}_{\\omega} is increased by \\Delta p; otherwise, p^{b}_{\\omega} is increased by \\Delta p."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":"No fixed numeric or symbolic input parameter is needed for the retained formal expressions. The price increment and case-study parameter values belong to the source's negotiation evidence and are not used in these termination or uniqueness conditions."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-validation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E10","quote":"The agents reach mutual agreement on a set of agreed contracts and contract prices through an iterative price-negotiation mechanism. At each step of the market, agents select their favorite bundle of available upstream and downstream contracts, and over-demanded contracts have their prices increased."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e24","quote":"The negotiation is complete when no price changes occur during an iteration."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","quote":"Each contract specifies the same energy quantity of demand reduction, but an agent may accept multiple contracts for each time interval. The contracts discretize the prosumers’ energy flexibility (in terms of energy and time), and allow each discrete unit to be individually priced."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","quote":"where X' is feasible if each trade \\omega \\in \\tau(X') is associated with at most one contract, and therefore has a unique price."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"b6bbd263bc7b7af70d25be3b50aeac3e05748a33814ce3963de52bfbedfb7719","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Two frozen constraints receive source-supported expressions: the no-price-change negotiation termination condition and the at-most-one-contract/unique-price feasibility condition. The individual-pricing statement remains qualitative and is not assigned an invented formula. The supplied B evidence is unreviewed; this patch does not assert independent source audit.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-x001","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001"],"rationale":"The buyer price is part of the iterative price signal coordinated into the local pricing outcome; edge E001 links coordination.price_signal to pricing.local for this rule."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-x002","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001"],"rationale":"The seller price is part of the iterative price signal coordinated into the local pricing outcome; edge E001 links coordination.price_signal to pricing.local for this rule."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-x003","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The selected feasible contract set is the object whose per-trade contract multiplicity determines the unique local contract price in C003."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001"],"rationale":"The termination expression records stability of the coordinated buyer and seller prices under the rule's existing price-signal link into local pricing."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C003","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The feasibility expression constrains the selected contract set that underlies local contract prices; no additional graph edge is asserted for this feasibility condition."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
